 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "외모 묘사 (be / have)",
   "en": "Describing appearance (be / have)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "키나 나이는 be + 형용사로 말합니다: She is tall. 머리나 눈은 have / has를 씁니다: She has long hair. 외모를 물을 때는 What does she look like?라고 합니다. 형용사는 명사 앞에 오고 복수형이 없습니다.",
   "en": "Height and age use be + adjective: She is tall. Hair and eyes use have / has: She has long hair. Ask about appearance with What does she look like? Adjectives go before the noun and have no plural form."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "be + 형용사",
     "She is tall."
    ],
    [
     "have / has + 명사",
     "He has brown eyes."
    ],
    [
     "형용사 + 명사",
     "long black hair"
    ],
    [
     "What ... look like?",
     "What does she look like?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "머리 색과 길이는 hair 앞에 씁니다: long black hair.",
    "en": "Colour and length go before hair: long black hair."
   },
   {
    "ko": "he / she에는 has를 씁니다.",
    "en": "With he / she use has."
   },
   {
    "ko": "short는 키와 머리 길이 모두에 쓸 수 있어요.",
    "en": "Short can describe height and hair."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
